    "objetivo": "Use «ci» for a place already named and for an idea, use «ne» for quantity and topic, and use «ci vuole», «ci vogliono» and «metterci» to say how long something takes. Avoid the English-speaker traps: dropping the pronoun, leaving it after the verb, and leaving out «ne» when the noun is gone.",
